refactor-text-clamping-and-centering

Refactored the text display for menu items and product cards to correctly handle multi-line truncation and vertical alignment.

Problem:
- Text in menu items and product cards with long names was not being truncated correctly.
- There was a requirement to have a fixed height (2 lines for menu, 3 for products) and vertically center text if it was shorter, while truncating if it was longer.
- A pure CSS solution was not possible without conflicting behaviors (good truncation vs. vertical alignment).

Solution:
- Modified the dynamic HTML generation in JavaScript (`render.js` and `ready.js`).
- Wrapped the text content of `.menu_item_name` (categories) and `.flex_row_item_name` (products) in a `<span>` element.
- Updated `style.css`:
    - The parent `div` (`.menu_item_name`, `.flex_row_item_name`) is now a flex container to handle vertical centering (`display: flex`, `align-items: center`).
    - The new inner `<span>` uses `-webkit-line-clamp` to correctly truncate text after 2 or 3 lines, respectively.

This change successfully implements the complex display requirements for both elements across the application.